Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj was one of the greatest rulers and warriors in Indian history. 
He was born on 19 February 1630 at Shivneri Fort. His mother, Jijabai, taught him courage, justice, and good values. Shivaji Maharaj established the Maratha 
Empire and fought against powerful enemies with great bravery and intelligence. 
He introduced strong administration, promoted the welfare of farmers, and respected people o
f all religions. He was also known for his excellent military strategies and fort management.
In 1674, he was crowned as Chhatrapati at Raigad Fort. Shivaji Maharaj is remembered as a symbol of courage, 
leadership, justice, and self-respect.
